 "sentences": [
  {
   "text": "Trump announced he beat Japan on tariffs.",
   "start": 0.0,
   "end": 2.22,
   "part": 1
  },
  {
   "text": "Instead, that tariff funded Japan's chip empire, and cost America a hundred and twenty-two billion dollars.",
   "start": 2.72,
   "end": 8.32,
   "part": 1
  },
  {
   "text": "Auto parts taxes compounded against Detroit.",
   "start": 8.32,
   "end": 10.76,
   "part": 1
  },
  {
   "text": "But look at what nobody explained.",
   "start": 11.34,
   "end": 12.64,
   "part": 1
  },
  {
   "text": "When you buy an American truck, its parts cross the border six separate times.",
   "start": 13.14,
   "end": 17.02,
   "part": 1
  },
  {
   "text": "An engine block from Ontario carries a twenty-five percent border tariff on raw parts.",
   "start": 17.52,
   "end": 21.56,
   "part": 1
  },
  {
   "text": "A wiring harness from Mexico gets hit with the exact same twenty-five percent.",
   "start": 22.06,
   "end": 25.58,
   "part": 1
  },
  {
   "text": "In the left lane, a taxed Toyota.",
   "start": 25.58,
   "end": 27.78,
   "part": 1
  },
  {
   "text": "In the right, a bankrupt Detroit.",
   "start": 27.78,
   "end": 29.74,
   "part": 1
  },
  {
   "text": "Toyota crosses once.",
   "start": 30.24,
   "end": 31.3,
   "part": 1
  },
  {
   "text": "Tokyo pays a flat fifteen percent on the sticker, not a penny more.",
   "start": 31.8,
   "end": 34.86,
   "part": 1
  },
  {
   "text": "But here's where the math breaks Detroit.",
   "start": 35.36,
   "end": 36.68,
   "part": 1
  },
  {
   "text": "On a thirty thousand dollar car, Tokyo pays forty-five hundred dollars in tariffs.",
   "start": 37.18,
   "end": 40.68,
   "part": 1
  },
  {
   "text": "Detroit pays over six thousand dollars in stacked border duties alone, right here at home.",
   "start": 41.18,
   "end": 45.02,
   "part": 1
  },
  {
   "text": "And that's where Tokyo pulled the second lever.",
   "start": 45.52,
   "end": 47.12,
   "part": 1
  },
  {
   "text": "Instead of reinvesting in America, Japan started dumping United States Treasuries.",
   "start": 47.68,
   "end": 51.12,
   "part": 1
  },
  {
   "text": "They sold a hundred and twenty-two billion dollars of Washington's debt.",
   "start": 51.62,
   "end": 54.38,
   "part": 1
  },
  {
   "text": "Tokyo brought that money home, pledging ten trillion yen to build domestic semiconductors.",
   "start": 54.88,
   "end": 59.64,
   "part": 1
  },
  {
   "text": "In finance, we call this the double squeeze:",
   "start": 60.22,
   "end": 62.08,
   "part": 1
  },
  {
   "text": "The competitor got cheaper parts and built silicon.",
   "start": 62.68,
   "end": 65.08,
   "part": 1
  },
  {
   "text": "And then we wrote them a blank check anyway, to bribe them to keep buying bonds.",
   "start": 65.64,
   "end": 68.62,
   "part": 1
  },
  {
   "text": "And this is where the policy backfired.",
   "start": 69.12,
   "end": 70.5,
   "part": 1
  },
  {
   "text": "Washington signed a tariff.",
   "start": 71.1,
   "end": 72.12,
   "part": 1
  },
  {
   "text": "Then Tokyo checked the Treasury vault.",
   "start": 72.74,
   "end": 74.44,
   "part": 1
  },
  {
   "text": "America used the tariff to tax its own cars, while Tokyo funded its own chips.",
   "start": 74.94,
   "end": 78.76,
   "part": 1
  }
 ],
 "edit_pauses_applied": false
}